{"title":"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the real solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> to the system of equations\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3decaf5b445e7348db6621ea63f55d5ad87744f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-3xy^2=-610,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a996490ffca4e780b0144c7d89f1d89989b772be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x^2y-y^3=182.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3f29b14edc9f8236a0524664ce3ddc2e5733310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+yi)^3 = x^3 + 3x^2yi + 3xy^2i^2 + y^3i^3 = (x^3-3xy^2) + (3x^2y-y^3)i = -610 + 182i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"656\" height=\"19\" /> \n</p><p>So, we need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/f/d5f75e4c3308879b4be3f657532bac5233cea3e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+yi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb64069e2c4276dce0d2ec6e8ed489aae618c0c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+yi)^3 = -610 + 182i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"19\" />. Even though there are three solutions, for simplicity, lets assume that one exists in the first quadrant in the complex plane, and try to find that one. \n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/1330973b35d84c289fdebb0f40c0f7257165e7ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|(x+yi)^3|^2 = (-610)^2 + (182)^2 = 372100 + 33124 = 405224 = 8 \\cdot 50653 = 2^3 \\cdot 37^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"641\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/3/4c371a7b2da94a2be41bfb47f481852ac9044425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x+yi|^2 = \\sqrt[3]{2^3 \\cdot 37^3} = 2\\cdot37 = 74$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"268\" height=\"22\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a189c277f6cef018e93d372484c103b5cdeb63d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 74$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1acd198a59821110c1234d23fd8b55f346b06ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y) = ( 5,7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d388db7aa14bd2737621f3db4b897e9e63ec4ea0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> are the only positive integer solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a189c277f6cef018e93d372484c103b5cdeb63d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 74$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />. (Even though the solution may be non-integral, this is a good place to start.) \n</p><p>However, letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/f/98f8bafd17af0ee162078e9931991a519fc9a4c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\cdot cis(\\theta) = x+yi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />, [<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/8/b187363c68ae63b49065f312d59d37df2c64fb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+yi)^3 = r^3 \\cdot cis(3\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" />] and bounding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yields:  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96f3c0d28b6cabe120a3fc50a3a6efc72428dbf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 &lt; \\tan{(3\\theta)} = -\\dfrac{182}{610} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"211\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e4552ea6c0ef65aed8119f1f109628a72a6984b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$135^\\circ &lt; 3\\theta &lt; 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />. (Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f34abb1905779a6fa2c98b8994448b09bd6a213e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\theta$\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is obviously in the 2nd quadrant).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cacadcd2d013f0e67edd0507757a8c6977897f94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ &lt; \\theta &lt; 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a01b17574e6b1cd04f77dfbd418826295105aee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{(\\theta)} &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b7ad4c34a3f2485fb4fd2342d49e605df553fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. So, the only remaining positive integer solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1095ee056aab1fe2d3bf6c0a79164794e257a23a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y) = (5,7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>As a quick check: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cf6eb925424494a75ad9def42e8cc3f01e8686a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5+7i)^3 = (5)^3 + 3(5)^2(7)i + 3(5)(7)^2i^2 + (7)^3i^3 =  -610 + 182i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"500\" height=\"19\" /> \n</p><p>Thus, the solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/8223f579224876b471922b2cb9fd259b47fa2b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y) = \\boxed{(5,7)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"118\" height=\"29\" />. \n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef78f0e5a9ca50072a7955ad85f1a2d9a087a85e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5+7i)cis(120^\\circ) = \\left(\\dfrac{-5-7\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) + \\left(\\dfrac{-7+5\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"409\" height=\"53\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d17f366be4996b3d6b8939e34b55ad6159cf6e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5+7i)cis(240^\\circ) = \\left(\\dfrac{-5+7\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) + \\left(\\dfrac{-7-5\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"409\" height=\"53\" /> \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1a6a977dffc4a38e54664110856632a24ca0b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y) = \\left(\\dfrac{-5-7\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\dfrac{-7+5\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"264\" height=\"53\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/622428bda634eaf7ac2007071d3b3f7560862d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\dfrac{-5+7\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\dfrac{-7-5\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"197\" height=\"53\" /> are also solutions. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST\">2006 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b>15</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017211415\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 198/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1329/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 204/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5748/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.820      1 Template:ARML_box\n100.00%    7.820      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8022:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017211415 and revision id 31039. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}